 "notes_for_editor": "Thin on primary sources: no Lighthouse Board or Commissioner reports in the corpus for 1938-45, and no newspaper hits from Chronicling America for 1944. The 1944 hurricane account and 1963-67 crew anecdotes rest on LighthouseFriends (itself citing a 1944 Lincoln Journal piece and a 1967 article); a 1944 Boston Globe clipping on the USLHS site could not be read. Municipality differs between sources (NRHP: Bourne; USLHS: Pocasset; Wikipedia: Falmouth); story avoids naming one. NRHP and LF disagree slightly on build chronology (NRHP: construction 1940; transferred 18 Sept 1941). Keeper roster is the USLHS list (96 lines, 1942-1971) parsed mechanically; USCG lines are enlisted crew; 'Joseph Bowen' / 'Joseph H. Bowen' and Norbert P. Lambert appear in several lines. The 1915 Commissioner page number is a scan page (printed page marked uncertain). Hurricane date: story says September 1944; LF gives the lightship loss as early 15 Sept. Buyer not named (private person). Verifier 2026-10-27: 1915 buoy entry is on scan p.60 (appropriation text is on scan p.59, printed p.54); report is fiscal year ended 30 June 1915.",
